⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Table of Hours
node WE1 · WE1 · ⟦The Table of Hours:WE1:0501ab⟧

WHO   — The Table of Hours — life by the second
WHAT  — Taylorism made total: one timetable for a whole civilisation, with only a few ‘Personal Hours’ allowed.
WHERE — WE1 · WE  Framework inputs: We (Yevgeny Zamyatin, 1924)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the deepest standardisation is of time itself — schedule every minute and spontaneity dies quietly.
HOW   — By a master timetable governing waking, work, the march, the meal, and sex by pink ticket.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I tell a million people when to wake, eat, walk, and love — all at once, in step; spontaneity is the one thing I have no row for.

